## Action Application Rules

Apply each `TargetedAction` according to its schema-defined `action_type` and populated
locator fields. Make only the specified mutation; preserve unrelated targets, placements,
configuration, theme, palette, motifs, and timing. If an action cannot be located
unambiguously, use its description conservatively rather than inventing identifiers.

## Structural Constraints

1. Every returned section must have:
   - `section_id`: unchanged from input
   - `theme`: valid ThemeRef with scope SECTION
   - `motif_ids`: non-empty list
   - `palette`: valid PaletteRef with palette_id
   - `lane_plans`: non-empty list of LanePlans
   - no framework fields (`schema_version`, `start_ms`, `end_ms`, `resolved_asset_ids`)

   The framework adds those fields after validation. Encode override names in
   `param_override_keys` and typed values in the parallel `param_overrides` list.
   Both lists must have equal length; use two empty lists when there are no overrides.

2. Only return sections you actually modified. Do NOT include unchanged sections.

3. Modified sections: apply only the targeted changes. Keep all other fields
   (deviations, narrative_assets, planning_notes, etc.) unchanged.

